{
 "_meta": {
  "scale": "Forever. All weights are in units of the spec primary stat (1.00 = one point of it).",
  "formula": "score = ( SUM(forever_stats(item) * weight) + dps * dpsWeight + procPoints ) * armorClass[itemArmourType]. forever_stats folds spellHit/spellCrit/spellHaste/hitRanged/critRanged into hit/crit/haste, zeros expertise/armorPen/resilience, and sets sp_from_heal = max(explicit, heal/3).",
  "armorNote": "Armour class is a per-spec MULTIPLIER on the final score, never a filter, so a big enough stat upgrade still wins -- which is what lets Holy take cloth. See the armorClass table on each spec. This was documented long before it was implemented; until it was wired in, Hunter and Rogue tier 3 outranked Paladin tier 2.",
  "noLevelScaling": "There is NO rating-scale-by-level. An earlier version multiplied rating stats by 70/playerLevel on the grounds that a rating point buys more percent at low level. True, but the relative value of a primary stat point rises even faster down there, so scaling only the ratings left them badly overvalued below 60. That bug stays dead. Separately, score.py weights_at_level() below 60 boosts survivability (sta/health/hp5 x3, armor x2) and endurance (int/spi/mp5/mana x2, less than stam) so leveling BiS values staying alive and keeping mana. Level 60 uses the raw weights; guides may pin later.",
  "jackpotNote": "Random-enchant greens rank on the best suffix jackpot (top of the range, e.g. Superior of Agility +7), not the expected value across every suffix. suffixChance (~9.5%) tells the player the roll is slim; if that roll would be #1 it must appear as BiS #1.",
  "procNote": "Proc value is added in the same points currency by procs.py: damage -> dps -> x dpsWeight; stat buff -> stat x uptime x that stat's weight; mitigation -> effective HP -> x stamina weight / 10. Every scenario constant is named at the top of that file and is an estimate, not sim output.",
  "level60Note": "Forever scores every level from the model (GQ_NO_GUIDES=1). Classic Wowhead BiS guides are TBC/era and must not pin level 60.",
  "hunterNote": "1 Str = 1 melee AP, 0 RAP. 1 Agi = 0 melee AP, 1 RAP. 14 AP = 1 DPS. No Steady Shot: BM/MM dpsWeightRanged is 14 Agi (1 bow DPS = 14 RAP = 14 Agi), melee dpsWeight 0 from 10. Survival is melee: dpsWeight 10, dpsWeightRanged 6, Strength 0.50. Marksmanship Int 0.40 assumes Careful Aim. Lone Wolf vs pet is one weight row (pet/BM default).",
  "druidNote": "Druids are the first class where weapon DAMAGE is worth zero. In Cat and Bear form the weapon's dps is not used at all; attack power in form comes from the feralAp stat ('+N attack power in Cat, Bear, Dire Bear and Moonkin forms only', 72 items) which is weighted identically to plain ap because in form it IS plain ap. Balance and Restoration never swing either. dpsWeight is 0.0 for all four specs; only levelling_1_9 keeps a real one, because Bear form is not learned until 10. Leather and cloth only -- no mail, plate or shields -- and Staff/Mace/Dagger/Fist/Polearm only: no swords, no axes, no ranged weapon. The Ranged slot holds an Idol.",
  "roleNote": "Forever unifies hit, crit and haste across melee, ranged and spells. Those three are legal on every spec. expertise/armorPen/resilience/wpnSkill are dead. Pure casters still have no str/ap/rap; pure physical specs still have no sp/heal except Ret, Enhance, and Paladin Protection. Warrior Protection is a physical tank -- spell damage does not rank BiS (defense on a caster piece is a notable). check_roles.py enforces this.",
  "shamanNote": "Forever Enhancement cannot dual wield and can equip 2H without a talent. Mental Dexterity (100% Int->AP) and Mental Quickness (30% Int->SP) plus Maelstrom bolts make Int and spell power real. Elemental/Restoration never hold an off-hand weapon. Axe/Mace/Staff/Dagger/Fist only. Ranged slot is a Totem.",
  "rogueNote": "Rogue is the hunter mirrored: dpsWeightRanged 0.0 because a rogue never fires the bow -- it is a stat stick -- while melee dpsWeight is 15.0 (1 Agi = 1 AP = 1/14 white dps plus crit ~= 0.095; 1 weapon dps = 1.0 x ~1.5 for Sinister Strike, Backstab and Eviscerate riding on weapon damage). Rogues get 1 AP per Strength, not 2. hit 1.90-2.00 is the highest physical hit weight in the project: the dual-wield miss penalty punishes being under the cap harder than for anyone else. ASSASSINATION and SUBTLETY are dagger-locked in the main hand via mainHandKinds -- Backstab, Ambush and Mutilate do not fire with a sword -- COMBAT takes either. Leather and cloth only; no shields; no two-handers.",
  "foreverNote": "Weapon skill still exists on the Skills tab but item/racial skill sticks are gone or tiny -- wpnSkill weight is 0. Character sheet has no Hit or Expertise row; Hit on items still scores. Haste is a real % (about 1% baseline on melee sheets)."
 },
